      "prompt": "A railway bypass switch forms a transversal intersecting two parallel tracks. Two consecutive interior angles along the crossing track have algebraic measures of $(3x + 20)^\\circ$ and $(2x + 10)^\\circ$, which sum to a straight line measure of $180^\\circ$. Determine the measure of the larger obtuse interior angle in degrees.",
      "display": "(3x + 20)^\\circ + (2x + 10)^\\circ = 180^\\circ",
      "plainText": "(3x + 20) + (2x + 10) = 180",
      "answerDisplay": "110",
      "answerPlain": "110",
      "givens": {
        "coeff_a": 3,
        "const_a": 20,
        "coeff_b": 2,
        "const_b": 10,
        "straight_sum": 180
      },
      "trapGivens": [
